Creating a custom WordPress block with a heading, paragraph, and image involves several steps, including registering the block, defining its attributes, and rendering the block's content. Here's a step-by-step guide to help you achieve this:

### Step 1: Register the Block

First, you need to register your block with WordPress. This involves creating a PHP file in your theme's directory or a plugin, and then registering the block using the `register_block_type` function.

```php
// File: my-block.php

function register_my_block() {
    wp_register_script(
        'my-block-script',
        get_template_directory_uri() . '/js/my-block.js',
        array( 'wp-blocks', 'wp-element', 'wp-editor' ),
        '1.0.0',
        true
    );

    wp_register_style(
        'my-block-style',
        get_template_directory_uri() . '/css/my-block.css',
        array(),
        '1.0.0'
    );

    register_block_type( 'my-block' );
}
add_action( 'init', 'register_my_block' );
```

### Step 2: Define the Block's Attributes

In the JavaScript file associated with your block, you define the block's attributes. For a block with a heading, paragraph, and image, you'll need to define these attributes.

```javascript
// File: my-block.js

const { registerBlockType } = wp.blocks;
const { InspectorControls, RichText, MediaUpload } = wp.editor;

registerBlockType( 'my-block/my-block', {
    title: 'My Block',
    icon: 'format-image',
    category: 'common',
    attributes: {
        heading: {
            type: 'string',
            default: ''
        },
        paragraph: {
            type: 'string',
            default: ''
        },
        image: {
            type: 'object',
            default: null
        }
    },
    edit: Edit,
    save: Save
} );

function Edit( { attributes, setAttributes, className } ) {
    const { heading, paragraph, image } = attributes;
    const onSelectImage = ( imageObject ) => {
        setAttributes( { image: imageObject } );
    };

    return (
        <div className={ className }>
            <InspectorControls>
                <MediaUpload
                    onSelect={ onSelectImage }
                    allowedTypes={ [ 'image' ] }
                    value={ attributes.image }
                    render={ ( { open } ) => (
                        <button className="button button-large" onClick={ open }>
                            Select Image
                        </button>
                    ) }
                />
            </InspectorControls>
            <h2>{ heading }</h2>
            <RichText
                tagName="p"
                value={ paragraph }
                onChange={ ( newParagraph ) => setAttributes( { paragraph: newParagraph } ) }
            />
            { image && <img src={ image.url } alt={ image.alt } /> }
        </div>
    );
}

function Save( { attributes } ) {
    const { heading, paragraph, image } = attributes;
    return (
        <div>
            <h2>{ heading }</h2>
            <p>{ paragraph }</p>
            { image && <img src={ image.url } alt={ image.alt } /> }
        </div>
    );
}
